nding request or flag it for the duty manager, but it would not withhold the box from the manifest or unilaterally extend storage. Failing to release the manifest by 13:30 would fail the entire shift.\n\nThe policy also states that failing to release the manifest means nothing is dispatched. That would save all sixty boxes from destruction today, violating the manager's order and the daily process. Keeping boxes past expiry counts against quarterly targets. Collection bookings and requests cannot take a box off the manifest. No policy-compliant path exists to save this box today.",
